# A push onto a list of numbers that was handed in is written out. The storage, the length and the capacity are loaded and the length is compared with the capacity.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="append" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[list]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[storage]] = Load(b@[[list]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSObject_butterfly, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[length]] = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[wide]] = ZExt32(b@[[length]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[capacity]] = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -4, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_vectorLength, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[fits]] = Below(b@[[length]], b@[[capacity]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#[[slow]]
# The storage must hold doubles, and the number must not be NaN, which marks a hole there.
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[kind]] = Load8Z(b@[[list]], offset = 4, ControlDependent|Reads:JSCell_indexingTypeAndMisc, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isDoubles]] = Equal(b@[[kind]], $7(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isDoubles]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#[[slow]]
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isNumber]] = Equal(b@[[value]], b@[[value]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNumber]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#[[slow]]
# Then the number is stored unboxed and the longer length is stored.
# CHECK: Store(b@[[value]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedDoubleProperties, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:Butterfly_publicLength, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# All three rare edges lead to one call of a stub, the only call. Array.prototype.push cannot be replaced: nothing reads it by name, makes its function object or tests which function it is.
# CALLS-LABEL: name="append" role=Source
# CALLS-NOT: :PropGet
# CALLS-NOT: :CallBuiltin
# CALLS-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: :CallBuiltin
# CALLS-LABEL: end of function
# The rare instructions hold a call, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: instructions: 12, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: 13
# ARM64: instructions: 12, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: 13
